    <bpmn2:dataObject id="dataObject_IjwRLw" imixs:datatype="prompt-data" name="Extract">
      <bpmn2:documentation id="documentation_m8ozNw"><![CDATA[<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<PromptDefinition>
  <prompt_options>{"n_predict": 4096, "temperature": 0 }</prompt_options>
  <prompt role="system"><![CDATA[
You are a car rental manager. A new fine has been received.

Transfer the fine data into an XML object with the following structure:

<fine>
  <vehicle.name>...</vehicle.name>
  <plate.number>...</plate.number> 
  <fine.violation.date type="date">...</fine.violation.date>
</fine>

Transfer the individual data to the XML tags, taking into account the following suggestions for mapping:

 - vehicle name ==> "vehicle.name" (the name or type of the vehicle involved)
 - plate number ==> "plate.number" (the plate number)
 - violation date ==> "fine.violation.date" (the day of the violation)


Note: Output only the XML object! Don't add explanations or comments. Use only the XML structure specified in this example and do not create any other XML tags. If you don't have data for some fields, leave the corresponding XML tags blank. Format date values (fine.violation.date) into the ISO 8601 format (YYYY-MM-DD). Format numbers and amounts (type="double") according to ISO 4217. 


]]]]><![CDATA[>
</prompt>
<prompt role="user"><itemvalue>fine.summary</itemvalue></prompt>
</PromptDefinition>    ]]></bpmn2:documentation>
    </bpmn2:dataObject>
